## SEVERITY / VERDICT
*Blocker:* a path beyond the two; a product diff other than the one import and one call; a word changed; `edge-trim.ts`, `client.ts` or the Customers page touched; a removed line or lost test name; a skip, `.only`, environment gate or sleep in an added row; **any PR check-run failed (the `web build` failure stands as a Blocker until its cause is read and it is green or proven a base fact), or either `api on SQL Server` shard not `completed` `success`**; a raw non-ASCII byte in an added line; a ticket key, card id or person name in an added line or commit message; a secret; a new open alert; the head moved; a parity cell where launcher and Customers page differ. *Major:* a non-equivalent mutant surviving (E6b or E6c surviving, or E6 refuted); a builder claim contradicted (57 rows, 32 red at main, 15 of 16, 2666 -> 2723, 0 names lost); a new row that no mutant turns red and is not a declared control; a repeat red; the ruling's set misread. *Minor/Note:* the missing 120-cap row in the builder's claim set; two commits where one was expected (lint fix, explained); the `signin-budget` timing flake; CI timing; the sibling `trim()` list.
**Round 1 of 2.** A NO GO sends a fix round to a new builder seat on this branch: state the fix-shape in prose and the ONE-line question for the product owner only if a ruling is needed; a second NO GO on the same class of finding is not a round 3 (it goes to the product owner). A GO or GO WITH FINDINGS lets Tuesday land #205 once the checks are green.

